{
  "about": "Fork addition (plan 44): what known apps need to be told to work behind Cosmos, on any port and under several names. Data, not code: read by src/behind/apps.go, checked by apps_test.go; every entry was tried with the real image behind a test Cosmos on HTTPS port 2053 under a .local-style and a domain-style name on the day 'checked' (version in 'version'), and cites the app's own documentation or code in 'source'. 'images': names without registry and tag (none for a dev server, which is recognised by its answer). 'appOwnHost': the URL tells the app its own address as Host and the public one in X-Forwarded-Host/-Port/-Proto (what the app's nginx guide asks: Host $proxy_host); 'noOwnHost': never (the app compares Origin with Host only, or builds redirects from Host). 'env': variables that tell the app its address; values may use {url} (the URL's public address, https://name:port), {urls} (every public address of the app's URLs, comma separated), {host}/{hosts} (name:port), {name}/{names}, {port}, {proxy} (the address the app sees Cosmos at); 'contains': what the variable must contain; 'when': always (sign-in or links fail without it), refused (only when the app refuses), ifSet (only when the container has it and it lacks the address). 'file': lines of the app's own configuration file ('section' where they go; 'images' when the file's place differs by image), 'when' refused or advice (works without, better with). 'signatures': how the app refuses (status, 'body' a pattern on the answer's text with its tags removed, 'log' a pattern on its log while it was asked; 'example' a real answer). Never a switch that turns an app's own host or CSRF check off: the apps are told the truth. Generic refusals of unknown apps are in check.go.",
